 "definition": "A TCP technique that reduces the number of small packets sent by holding back small writes until earlier data has been acknowledged.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A way of making TCP/IP networks more efficient by reducing the number of packets sent. It addresses the 'small-packet problem', where an application sends tiny chunks of data and each carries a large header overhead. Defined by John Nagle in 1984.",
